This is a short introduction to the usage of the Jupiter code dedicated to the classification of the cells segmented on 
non-linear excitation images. 
It requires that the NLM image has been analyzed by means of QuPath so to obtain the "Measurement file" that is the output of 
the "Sho Deterction Measurement" tool. It also requires that an average Binary Feature Vector is defined for as many cell types as possible. 

